== Method chosen by the tester (no steps in the DB)
Fibre pluggable in the x230: port1.0.4 AT-SPSX (1000BASE-SX, 850 nm, S/N A03240R151300357) <-> stack port1.0.3 AT-SPSX
(A03240R192701669), multimode LC-LC, x230 VLAN 104 / stack VLAN 104 (re-triage 10:00: "C ... 1000BASE-SX only").
1000BASE-SX has exactly one speed, 1000 Mb/s full duplex. So the case checks:
  (1) the supported speed: 1000 full with autoneg (`speed auto`, default) and fixed (`speed 1000`), link up, frames passing;
  (2) the unsupported speeds/duplex the CLI parser offers (it is media-blind: 10..400000): the x230 must not bring the SX
      link up at a speed the module cannot run -- either reject the command or leave the port at 1000 / down, never report
      a link at a speed the optic cannot carry.
Frames-passing evidence: the stack's loop-protection sends a loop-detect frame out port1.0.3 every 1 s and both ends send
LLDP every 30 s, so the input counter on each end must rise while the link is really up.

