== Summary
PROVEN: the AT-SPSX on the x230 runs its supported speed, 1000 full, both with autoneg and fixed; 10 / 2500 / 10000 and half
  duplex are rejected cleanly.
FAILED: `speed 100` and `speed auto 100` are accepted on the 1000BASE-SX module; the x230 then reports the port "connected
  a-full 100" while the link passes no frames either way (counters flat, LLDP lost) and the partner still sees 1000. A user
  gets a dead link that the switch reports as up. The IE520 behaves the same way (control), so this is probably shared AW+
  code; the expected behaviour is the "% Unsupported speed/duplex combination" the x230 already gives for 10 Mb/s.

Run: clean.
VERDICT: FAIL -- supported speed (1000 full, auto and fixed) works and 10/2500/10000/half are rejected, but `speed 100` / `speed auto 100` is accepted on the 1000BASE-SX module and the port reports "connected a-full 100" while passing no frames (counters flat 40 s, LLDP lost); the IE520 does the same
